hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"969","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sadafi informed me, Jabir ibn Ismail informed me, on the authority of Aqeel ibn Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, like the hadith of Ali bin Hussein, means that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he was hurried on his journey one day, he would join the noon prayer.” And the afternoon prayer, and if he wants to travel on the night he combines the sunset and the evening prayers, he delays the noon prayer until the beginning of the afternoon time, then he combines them and delays the afternoon prayer. Maghrib, until he combines it with dinner when twilight disappears.”"
"970","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb and Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, they said: Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, He said: I was with Abdullah bin Omar, Hafs bin Asim, and Musahaq bin Amr. He said: Then the sun set, and it was said to Ibn Omar: Prayer. He said: So he walked. It was said to him: Prayer, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “if he hastened on his journey, he would delay this prayer,” and I want to delay it. He said: We walked until midnight, or close to midnight. He said: Then he came down and prayed it. Abu Bakr said: In this report and Ibn’s report. Shihab, on the authority of Anas, it has been proven that combining the noon and afternoon prayers at the time of the afternoon prayer, and between the sunset and evening prayers at the time of the evening prayer After the disappearance of twilight, it is permissible, not according to what some Iraqis said: The combination of the noon and afternoon prayers is that the noon prayer is performed at the end of its time and the afternoon prayer at the end of the time. At the beginning of its time, and Maghrib at the end of its time before the twilight sets, and every prayer in a city or a travel is permissible according to them to be prayed according to what they explained. Combining the two prayers, as it is permissible according to them for the resident to pray all the prayers, if he likes, at the end of their time, and if he wishes, at the beginning of their time."
